==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|vrosch|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|frosc||frog|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*fruskaz||frog}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*prew-||jump, hop}}. Cognate with {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|vorsch||frog|lang=gml}}, Dutch {{m|nl|vors}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|froask}}, Icelandic {{m|is|froskur}}, English {{term|frosh||frog|lang=en}}. More at {{l|en|frosh}}.

